      "criterion": "sequencing",
      "details": "Actual independent content review by /root/lesson_content_review_2; report SHA256 cb8d6b0d43665af39b8757f456bc312c08152c5ac895d2e21e6047a015afeac4; original target lesson.md#successful-result-checkpoint. Owner acceptance does not resolve this advisory.",
      "excerpt": "Read short situations about practical problems, such as opening a document, connecting a printer, or preparing a room. Identify which sentence reports that the task eventually worked. Then explain briefly what result was achieved.",
      "explanation": "The successful-result, task-to-person, change-perspective, diagnose-difficulty, and expression-repair checkpoints give activity directions without their exercises or concrete items. Integrated practice and final retrieval are also instructions without exercise placements. All sixteen exercise references occur only in the final Repetisjon section. Learners therefore encounter repeated directions to perform unavailable tasks and receive the actual controlled practice only after all teaching and retrieval prose.",
